Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: use identity default domain for SM8650 MDSS

Add SM8650 MDSS to the existing display-client identity-domain list.
Retain access to inherited display buffers before native DRM attaches its
own paging domain, matching the existing handling of other Qualcomm display
clients. This removed early splash-buffer translation faults in SM8650 tests.

--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -414,6 +414,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8150-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8250-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-mdss" },
 	{ }
 };
